From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vkd3d-crossover <noreply@vkd3d-crossover.invalid>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] feat: hide non-blendable R9G9B9E5 render targets under
 VKD3D_RELAX_CAPS
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Not documented in OVERVIEW.md or NOTES.md; facts below come from the code
comment only.

Problem: shared-exponent render targets render on MoltenVK but cannot blend
natively and are very slow, while engines treat them as an optional fast path.

Root cause: the Vulkan format reports COLOR_ATTACHMENT without
COLOR_ATTACHMENT_BLEND for R9G9B9E5 on Apple GPUs.

Fix: with VKD3D_RELAX_CAPS set and no blend support for the format,
CheckFeatureSupport(FORMAT_SUPPORT) stops reporting R9G9B9E5_SHAREDEXP as a
render target, so applications take their standard (e.g. R11G11B10 /
RGBA16F) path. Inactive once MoltenVK reports blending for the format
(M7, N§20).

Verified by: no record in OVERVIEW.md / NOTES.md.

Off switch: VKD3D_ALLOW_R9G9B9E5_RT (any value), or unset VKD3D_RELAX_CAPS.
---
 libs/vkd3d/device.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libs/vkd3d/device.c b/libs/vkd3d/device.c
index 19223df..21081dc 100644
--- a/libs/vkd3d/device.c
+++ b/libs/vkd3d/device.c
@@ -4406,6 +4406,13 @@ static HRESULT d3d12_device_get_format_support(struct d3d12_device *device, D3D1
                 }
             }
         }
+        /* Shared-exponent render targets are rare on native D3D12 hardware, so engines treat them as an optional
+         * fast path. On MoltenVK (Apple GPUs) they render but cannot blend natively and are very slow; hide them
+         * so applications take their standard (e.g. R11G11B10 / RGBA16F) path. */
+        if (data->Format == DXGI_FORMAT_R9G9B9E5_SHAREDEXP && vkd3d_relax_caps() && !getenv("VKD3D_ALLOW_R9G9B9E5_RT") &&
+                !(image_features & VK_FORMAT_FEATURE_2_COLOR_ATTACHMENT_BLEND_BIT))
+            image_features &= ~(VK_FORMAT_FEATURE_2_COLOR_ATTACHMENT_BIT | VK_FORMAT_FEATURE_2_COLOR_ATTACHMENT_BLEND_BIT);
+
         if (image_features & VK_FORMAT_FEATURE_2_COLOR_ATTACHMENT_BIT)
         {
             data->Support1 |= D3D12_FORMAT_SUPPORT1_RENDER_TARGET | D3D12_FORMAT_SUPPORT1_MULTISAMPLE_RENDERTARGET;
